# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=flasks spec=hunter:marksmanship style=flee
# size=25 difficulty=heroic view=390x844,touch save=fresh. `boss=flasks` is a
# coverage label only -- `evening` steers at no boss, the walk starts at the
# door same as any other.
#
# A fresh save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before, checked against sessions.jsonl and
# direction.md first: hunter:marksmanship has only ever appeared in
# battleground and daily-mode pulls (grep confirms), never inside an evening
# at all. flee has been given to an evening three times before (priest:
# discipline and druid:guardian at 10-normal, both stalling THE VIGIL; shaman:
# restoration at 25-heroic, crossing THE VIGIL clean then stalling THE WEST
# CLIMB) -- all three were healer or tank roles. This is the first flee-style
# evening on a pure ranged dps, and the first at 25-heroic on any dps role at
# all. flee never calls an ability (only ever moves away from danger), so a
# marksmanship hunter under it deals zero damage the whole evening by
# construction -- the question is only what that costs the raid at heroic/25,
# where direction.md's line 1 has so far shown a tank and two healers getting
# carried for free but never a dps specifically inside a full evening walk
# (only inside single mode=raid pulls).
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:hunter:marksmanship
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening flee 260 6
state
shot end
says
bill
